cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below and record the exact
  release (for example tetris-ballistic 1.2.x from PyPI) or the commit of
  main that you used.
title: 'tetris-ballistic: Monte Carlo simulation of Tetris ballistic deposition and other surface growth models'
type: software
authors:
- family-names: Chen
  given-names: Le
  affiliation: Auburn University
- family-names: Montes
  given-names: Mauricio
  affiliation: Auburn University
- family-names: Ruau
  given-names: Ian
  affiliation: Auburn University
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/chenle02/Simulations_on_Some_Surface_Growth_Models
url: https://simulations-on-some-surface-growth-models.readthedocs.io/main/
abstract: >-
  Python package for simulating ballistic deposition of Tetris pieces
  (the 19 fixed tetromino orientations and a 1x1 cell) on a one-dimensional
  substrate, with sticky and non-sticky contact rules, interface-height and
  roughness statistics, hole counts, image and animation output, and tools
  for KPZ scaling analysis of large simulation ensembles. It began as a
  final exam project for Math 7820 (Applied Stochastic Processes I),
  Fall 2023, at Auburn University.
keywords:
- surface growth
- ballistic deposition
- Tetris
- KPZ universality
- Monte Carlo simulation
- interacting particle systems
